      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Harden jq safe-bin semantics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators can explicitly configure exec safe bins for narrow stdin-oriented tools. `jq` is broader than that model: it can read environment data and load jq code through explicit modules and startup files, which means approval-free safe-bin execution cannot be constrained to the intended stdin-only behavior.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change makes `jq` fail closed in the safe-bin semantic gate, matching the existing treatment for other tools whose semantics cannot be validated to stdin-only. Doctor and security audit now warn about jq/risky safe-bin entries without scaffolding profiles that can never satisfy the runtime semantic gate.\n\nOperators can still run jq through an explicit allowlist entry or the normal approval prompt.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`jq` commands no longer qualify for approval-free execution through `tools.exec.safeBins`, even for simple field filters. Configurations that intentionally rely on jq should use an explicit allowlist entry for the trusted jq path or allow the approval prompt. Other safe-bin tools such as `head`, `tail`, `tr`, and `wc` are unchanged.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/exec-safe-bin-semantics.test.ts src/infra/exec-safe-bin-policy.test.ts src/infra/exec-approvals-safe-bins.test.ts src/infra/exec-safe-bin-runtime-policy.test.ts src/commands/doctor/shared/exec-safe-bins.test.ts src/security/audit-exec-safe-bins.test.ts src/infra/exec-approvals-config.test.ts src/infra/exec-approvals.test.ts`\n  - Result: 3 Vitest shards passed, 227 tests passed.\n  - Local fallback used because Testbox/Crabbox was unavailable in this environment: installed `crabbox` is `0.20.0`, while the Testbox wrapper requires a newer binary; direct AWS fallback also lacked broker configuration.\n- `review-pr` review-only artifacts validated for head `0fc1e1178a8e100e0d72b1cd4d76d6ea1717b67e`; findings: 0.\n- `autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main` passed for head `0fc1e1178a8e100e0d72b1cd4d76d6ea1717b67e`; no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
